      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is working not due to the death notification, but because killServer calls exit directly, and then it will return DEAD_OBJECT, and BpBinder transact sets mAlive\u003d0 in transact, which is why \u0027isBinderAlive\u0027 will return false.\n\nHowever, if this dies for other reasons, the test won\u0027t work.\n\nConsider these two alternative implementations, if you use either, you will see this test doesn\u0027t work until the change I suggested in the other comment:\n\n1. option one - kill the service in another thread. Change `FooBar::onTransact` to `std::thread([]{ exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }).detach();`. and then, this test will usually fail (and sometimes pass). By exiting asynchronously, it will show the death notification doesn\u0027t work.\n\n2. option two - kill the service by PID. You could remove \u0027killServer\u0027 and use:\n\n```\npid_t pid;\nASSERT_EQ(OK, binder1-\u003egetDebugPid(\u0026pid));\nsystem(\"kill -9 \" + std::to_string(pid));\n```\n\nThen, binder is out of the loop, so it won\u0027t work because of isBinderAlive.\n\n\n---\n\nFor more coverage, you could kill the service both ways, but it\u0027s more important to kill it asynchronously since linkToDeath will be tested then.",
